[25.152651, "o", "\u001b[2mLoaded Prisma config from prisma.config.ts.\r\n\u001b[22m\r\n"]
[25.286919, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[31m!\u001b[39m\u001b[22m unknown or unexpected option: --skip-generate\r\n\r\n🏋️  Create a migration from changes in Prisma schema, apply it to the database, trigger generators (e.g. Prisma Client)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mUsage\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[2m$\u001b[22m prisma migrate dev [options]\r\n\r\n  The datasource URL configuration is read from the Prisma config file (e.g., \u001b[3mprisma.config.ts\u001b[23m).\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mOptions\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n       -h, --help   Display this help message\r\n         --config   Custom path to your Prisma config file\r\n         --schema   Custom path to your Prisma schema\r\n         --url      Override the datasource URL from the Prisma config file\r\n       -n, --name   Name the migration\r\n    --create-only   Create a new migration but do not apply it\r\n                    The migration will be empty if there are no changes in Prisma schema\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mExamples\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  Create a migration from changes in Prisma schema, apply it to the database, trigger generators (e.g. Prisma Client)\r\n  \u001b[2m$\u001b[22m prisma migrate dev\r\n\r\n  Specify a schema\r\n  \u001b[2m$\u001b[22m prisma migrate dev --schema=./schema.prisma\r\n\r\n  Create a migration without applying it\r\n  \u001b[2m$\u001b[22m prisma migrate dev --create-only\r\n\r\n"]
[25.308124, "o", "⠙"]
[25.309804, "o", "\u001b[1G"]
[25.30983, "o", "\u001b[0K"]
